{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"2f045c27-ecf6-4851-8c65-226eb8f0db3a","runId":"f8399a50-bd9a-4d40-b21d-948f4b075ae1","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":13,"previousEventHash":"sha256:a8d771160158ae19ad208794f81a1ec25bf3708d454e48dc313b3bb940eff991","type":"phase.completed","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a04358-c969-7a5a-9b8c-48fd23aadf57","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-27T13:14:48.691Z","idempotencyKey":"phase:investigate:1:complete","payload":{"phase":"investigate","attempt":1,"evidence":[],"report":"<!-- FORGE:INVESTIGATOR -->\n## Investigation Report\n\n| Field | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| Verdict | Invalid |\n| Confidence | High |\n| Severity | Low |\n| Task Type | Security regression coverage |\n\n### What Was Claimed\n\n`GitHubIssueProjector.setWorkflowLabel` was reported to interpolate an unvalidated `issueNumber` into GitHub issue and label API paths.\n\n### What We Found\n\nThe frozen `staging` base already rejects non-positive and non-safe-integer issue numbers before transport use. `setWorkflowLabel` performs an explicit guard, and the shared `#replaceWorkflowLabel` path also calls `requireIssueNumber` before constructing either API path. The reported unsafe behavior is therefore not reproducible at `297621681ac15a325eed4d51903ada13c7330423`.\n\nFocused regression coverage is absent, so a narrow test should preserve the safety invariant and prove malformed runtime values never reach the transport.\n\n### Root Cause\n\nThe original review finding is stale relative to the frozen integration base: validation has already been restored in production code, but no focused test records the regression boundary.\n\n### Affected Files\n\n- `src/adapters/github-projection.ts` — already contains the positive safe-integer guard at the public and shared mutation boundaries.\n- `test/adapters/github-projection.test.ts` — lacks focused malformed-issue-number coverage for `setWorkflowLabel`.\n\n### Evidence\n\n- `setWorkflowLabel` rejects values for which `Number.isSafeInteger(issueNumber)` is false or `issueNumber < 1`.\n- `#replaceWorkflowLabel` calls `requireIssueNumber(issueNumber)` before constructing `/issues/${issueNumber}` and `/issues/${issueNumber}/labels`.\n- Existing projection tests exercise only valid issue number `42` for workflow label transitions.\n- The assigned worktree has no pre-existing diff.\n\n### History Findings\n\n- Issue #209 originated from security finding `security-001` on PR #199 at reviewed head `a618dbaf461e642818073a2a3c02a10c3c4e7b3`.\n- The frozen integration base now contains the missing validation, so only the regression-test gap remains actionable.\n\n### Recommendation\n\nAdd a focused adapter test that passes malformed runtime values through `setWorkflowLabel`, asserts the stable `TypeError`, and proves the transport is never called. Do not alter projector behavior that is already correct.\n\n### Related Issues\n\nNo linked source issue was recorded; PR #199 is the provenance supplied by issue #209.\n\n### Decomposition Assessment\n\nNo decomposition is required. The remaining work is a single focused regression test in one adapter test file.\n\n### Acceptance Spec\n\n- [x] Validate the finding against the frozen integration base.\n- [x] Confirm the existing production guard executes before path construction.\n- [ ] Add focused regression coverage for malformed runtime issue numbers.\n- [ ] Run the required `check` command.\n- [ ] Re-review the exact committed remediation head with correctness and security reviewers.\n\n<!-- INVESTIGATION:COMPLETE -->"}}
